PROTOCOL='**V41: three focused mechanism experiments**\n\nLocked before scientific execution, 10 September 2026. Four fresh seeds: 41101–41104. The three experiments have different estimands and are not pooled. This is a diagnostic round; four seeds cannot establish broad qualification. No scientific outcome triggers a larger run or a changed threshold.\n\nThe recovered latest chat recommendation proposed fixed-event utility eviction, lag/live/frozen stationarity, and SLOTS versus READ-HYBRID versus FULL-HYBRID. Its full wording and numerical settings were unavailable. The settings below are explicit implementation refinements, informed by the V40 audit, rather than a claim to reproduce an unseen protocol exactly. Earlier chat estimates are not reused as verified measurements.\n\n| Experiment | Purpose | Fixed workload per seed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Utility | Isolate the consequence of choosing which consolidated slots to evict | 48 identities; 320 contextual training-target presentations; 224 frozen followup targets |\n| Hybrid | Separate changing read predictions from changing admission/write history | 32 identities per wave ×4 waves; 8 repeats; 1,096 records =15,344 continuously scored/learned bytes |\n| Stationarity | Separate adaptive normalization from frozen normalization while output learning continues | Same 15,344-byte main stream plus4,088 causal warmup bytes;19,432 total |\n\n**Utility intervention.** Use the existing V40 base, exact traces, corroborated slots, utility ledger, and demotion semantics. The contextual assay supplies complete twelve-byte contexts and observes only their next byte; context bytes are covariates, not additional training events. Random six-byte keys and targets are paired with preassigned demand2/4/8; none of these evaluator identities/classes is an input to the eviction rule. All branches share one learned resident snapshot and one predeclared intervention time, after320 target observations.\n\nBefore intervention require at least16 resident slots, every resident having at least2 postbirth utility observations, and at least90% held-out acquisition. A failed seed reports task-invalid and performs no policy comparison. These gates were passed on a distinct full-size engineering seed before science. After the gate, evict floor(number of resident slots /4), once, under UTILITY-RATE, LFU-RATE, LRU, RANDOM, and SHUFFLED-UTILITY. Keep a no-eviction reference. Candidates, timestamps and victim counts match exactly. The shuffled control permutes the same utility multiset within postbirth-use bins × age quartiles; report changed-source and victim-overlap counts.\n\nThe base and all memories are frozen during the identical224-target held-out followup. Thus the policy difference is the immediate consequence of its victim set under fixed demand, not a claim about long-term recovery after further learning. Trained-alias and unseen-alias recall are reported separately. Demotion restores two exact traces and can INCREASE semantic bytes; this experiment tests consolidated-slot scarcity, not RAM savings. The followup’s repeated deterministic predictions do not create independent statistical units. Primary contrasts use future excess loss relative to no eviction and demand-weighted accuracy; compare utility with LFU, LRU, random and shuffled on the same seed. Also report unweighted held-out accuracy and trace/slot costs.\n\n**Hybrid split.** Retain the exact V39 slot rule and Claude V40 superposed mechanism. SLOTS and READ-HYBRID share literally the same physical slot memory and all writes. SLOTS falls back to base scores; READ-HYBRID substitutes superposition only when that same lookup has no authority. FULL-HYBRID is the original composition: superposition fallback also participates in post-outcome admission/confirmation, creating a separate memory history. SUPER and BASE are scoring references. No workload identity labels enter any learner.\n\nREAD minus SLOTS identifies a pure read substitution on a fixed shared history. FULL minus READ identifies the total downstream consequence of the changed memory history with the same fallback family; it does not isolate one individual admission event. Report whole/target/non-target loss, authority strata, admission/confirmation differences, checkpoint loss and occupancy, E1/E2, old seen/held-out recall, continued acquisition and revision. The loss decomposition telescopes exactly. Probes must leave the entire learner state unchanged. Omit stochastic controls whose previous implementations were invalid; this closure uses a deterministic shared-history counterfactual directly. No standalone compute-efficiency claim is made from shared execution. Incremental storage includes the superposed output and projection arrays. The4096-unit layer is retained to avoid adding a neuron-count change to this mechanism test.\n\n**Stationarity intervention.** Recover the original Claude V39 PhaseFront and lag_bits from its complete source (SHA2560f9577b4a06e1443f0ff38753f630a1a3df8bc7c6fca519f0efa997e820a78d0). Preserve those definitions. Correct historical lookahead by discovering period only from146 already observed disjoint warmup records, then fitting the normalizer on146 additional disjoint records. Both stages total4,088 next-byte events and are counted. During warmup output weights also learn. Clone the entire phase model at the warmup boundary. PHASE-LIVE continues normalizer and output updates; PHASE-FROZEN freezes normalizer statistics only and continues output updates. Both use identical advancing byte time. LAG remains the stationary reference; charged state budgets match with inert padding for the normalizer allowance. Report functional output/projection/normalizer bytes and padding separately.\n\nReport matched-phase fixed-context code overlap to measure normalizer drift, actual-time recurrent-context overlap to expose phase misalignment, separation geometry, online bits/byte, one-shot transfer, old recall, and later acquisition. A discovered period need not equal the record length; report it. Frozen-versus-live changes can include normalization geometry adaptation as well as removal of drift; the diagnostics distinguish these observed consequences without claiming causal mediation. Main and warmup-inclusive losses are separate. The shorter stream and causal warmup make this a new closure experiment, not a historical replication. No clutter or capacity sweep is added.\n\n**Execution and interruption.** One self-contained Python file embeds the historical sources and all three modules. Fixed plans lock source, protocol, configuration and seeds. Every32 completed records, save the complete learner, evaluator, input cursor, RNG, and accumulated metrics. A single checksummed checkpoint file is replaced atomically; a previous generation is retained. Corrupted checkpoints and mismatched source/plan identities are rejected. Existing completed records are checksum-verified and skipped. SIGINT/SIGTERM request a stop after the current block; the same command resumes. A process lock excludes concurrent writers. macOS caffeinate is automatic. Initial environment and each invocation are recorded. Intermediate results archives include checkpoints; completed archives omit large finished states. Persistence outside a replaced execution environment requires saving a snapshot separately, which the current execution workflow does.\n\n**Verification and analysis.** Distinct engineering seeds verify original numerical equivalence, probe invariance, continuing output plasticity after normalization freeze, exact victim budgets, ledger multiset matching, checkpoint/resume equality, corrupted-state rejection and changed-plan rejection. Engineering outputs are never scientific seeds. A paused smoke run must resume and a finished rerun must train zero new examples before science begins.\n\nUse seed-level paired differences, individual seed values, pointwise Student95% intervals and exact sign-reversal sensitivity. With four seeds, the smallest two-sided complete-sign-reversal p-value is0.125; no p<0.05 gate is attempted. If an assay fails its gate, report all failures and do not silently analyze a selected valid subset as a completed four-seed experiment. Results are conditional on these synthetic tasks. Preserve useful positive and negative mechanism evidence without declaring a general non-Transformer persistent learner solved.\n'
CONFIGS={'hybrid': {'keys_per_wave': 32, 'repeats': 8, 'trace_cap': 512, 'slot_cap': 384}, 'utility': {'smoke': False}, 'stationarity': {'keys_per_wave': 32, 'repeats': 8, 'units': 4096, 'active': 205, 'contacts': 12, 'discovery_records': 146, 'fit_records': 146}}
SMOKE_CONFIGS={'hybrid': {'keys_per_wave': 4, 'repeats': 2, 'trace_cap': 512, 'slot_cap': 384}, 'utility': {'smoke': True}, 'stationarity': {'keys_per_wave': 4, 'repeats': 2, 'units': 128, 'active': 7, 'contacts': 12, 'discovery_records': 20, 'fit_records': 20}}
SEEDS=(41101,41102,41103,41104)
